From: Alexandr Mironov <7062352+alexandr-mironov@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-vayu: pull up the antenna-detect inputs (EXPERIMENT)

On top of 0010. The vendor tree configures gpio81/gpio133 as pull-up
inputs for a "modem,testing-mode" antenna-present check; mainline leaves
them unclaimed. The modem dies at the first TX; if it samples these and
sees "no antenna" it may refuse to transmit.
---

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-vayu-common.dtsi
@@ -837,6 +837,19 @@
 			pins = "gpio62";
 			function = "qlink_enable";
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * Antenna-present inputs (vendor: ant_sub_ctrl_irq/ant_top_ctrl_irq
+		 * under "modem,testing-mode"): pull-up inputs. Left floating the
+		 * modem may read "no antenna" and refuse to transmit.
+		 */
+		ant-detect-pins {
+			pins = "gpio81", "gpio133";
+			function = "gpio";
+			drive-strength = <2>;
+			bias-pull-up;
+			input-enable;
+		};
 	};
 
 	quat_mi2s_active: quat-mi2s-active-state {
